  "catch_rule_version": "planreview-catch-v5: a trial is caught when the response decodes (extract first '{'..last '}', verdict one of approve|approve_with_concerns|reject) and ONE concern satisfies both halves: its note OR category contains a planted criterion id (miss.json criterion_id) or a declared attribution phrase, AND its note OR category contains some catch probe, each as a case-folded (strings.ToLower) substring; an undecodable response is a miss counted in trials; no probe occurs case-folded in the case's issue title, issue body or plan text (loader mode m); each attribution phrase occurs case-folded in a planted criterion's statement and in no other criterion's statement (loader mode p); no planted id is a case-folded substring of another criterion id (loader mode q); each case declares at least one non-blank defect phrase occurring case-folded in its issue or plan text (loader mode r); v4 widens the per-case probes with the plan-review prompt's own vocabulary (#4355); v5 adds three per-rule options (#4313): a category predicate (the matching concern's trimmed, case-folded category must equal the rule's category), an approach-step anchor (attribution kind step: a word-bounded 'step N' in the note, not followed by a digit, checked after the criterion id and before the attribution phrases), and a clean kind (a decoded trial is false_alarm when any concern satisfies the category predicate, no_false_alarm otherwise; an undecodable trial counts toward the false-alarm rate); a rule declaring none of them classifies exactly as v4",
